Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: No Traces Appearing
Symptoms: Jaeger UI shows no traces or empty results

Solutions:

Verify Istio proxy injection:
kubectl get pods -o wide
Ensure pods show 2/2 containers.

Check if traffic is reaching the services:
kubectl logs -f deployment/productpage-v1 -c istio-proxy
Verify Jaeger configuration:
kubectl get configmap istio -n istio-system -o yaml | grep -A 10 defaultConfig
Issue 2: Incomplete Traces
Symptoms: Traces show only some services, missing spans

Solutions:

Check service mesh configuration:
istioctl proxy-config cluster productpage-v1-xxx.default
Verify all services have Istio sidecars:
kubectl get pods --show-labels
Issue 3: Jaeger UI Not Accessible
Symptoms: Cannot access Jaeger UI on localhost:16686

Solutions:

Check port-forward process:
ps aux | grep port-forward
Restart port-forward:
pkill -f "port-forward.*jaeger"
kubectl port-forward -n istio-system svc/jaeger-query 16686:16686 &
Cleanup
Remove the fault injection rules:
kubectl delete virtualservice ratings
kubectl delete destinationrule ratings
Stop the port-forward process:
pkill -f "port-forward.*jaeger"
Optional - Remove the Bookinfo application:
kubectl delete -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.20/samples/bookinfo/platform/kube/bookinfo.yaml
kubectl delete -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.20/samples/bookinfo/networking/bookinfo-gateway.yaml
